NAME
       xxd - make a hex dump

SYNOPSIS
       xxd [-pu] [-c COLS] [-l LEN] [-s OFFSET] [FILE]

DESCRIPTION
       Print a hex dump of FILE or standard input: offset, bytes in hex and
       their printable characters. On a terminal printable bytes are green, NUL
       bytes gray and the rest red.

OPTIONS
       -c COLS
           bytes per line (default 16)

       -l LEN
           stop after LEN bytes

       -s OFFSET
           start at OFFSET

       -p
           plain continuous hex dump

       -u
           use upper case hex

EXAMPLES
       xxd /bin/ls | head
       xxd -l 64 -s 0x40 disk.img

SEE ALSO
       cat(1)
